# Shell scripts must be LF-only.
#
# CRLF breaks them on Linux in a way that fails silently rather than loudly:
# bash reads `set -euo pipefail\r` as the option "pipefail\r", rejects it with
# "invalid option name", and the script then continues with errexit DISABLED.
# Every "check this command's exit status" guarantee in these scripts silently
# evaporates while the script appears to work.
#
# The pattern has no slash, so it matches shell scripts at any depth and
# supersedes the narrower infrastructure/scripts/*.sh rule it replaces.
*.sh text eol=lf